course: dictionary
lesson: 14524
title: Perishable food
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some foods do not last long. A word for them is perishable, which means it goes bad or rotten quickly. The word perish means to be destroyed or to go off, so perishable food will spoil if you leave it out too long.
explain: «Milk is perishable, so keep it in the fridge.» Perishable is a describing word here. It tells you what kind of milk this is: milk that goes off quickly. Ask yourself what the word describes, and you will often find its meaning.
explain: The word can also be a noun in the plural: perishables. «The shop kept its perishables in the cold room.» Perishables are the foods and goods that go off quickly, such as milk, meat and fruit. Shops and lunch boxes keep them cool to stop them spoiling.
fact: Perishable means goes bad or rotten quickly.
fact: Milk, meat and fruit are common perishable foods.
fact: Perishable is an adjective, so it describes a noun, as in «perishable food». Perishables, with an s, is a plural noun meaning foods that go off quickly.
fact: Keep perishables chilled in the fridge, and check the use-by date.
fact: The opposite idea is a food that lasts a long time, such as tinned beans.
exercise: «Milk is perishable, so keep it in the fridge.» What does perishable mean? | Made of shiny plastic | Very heavy to carry | *Goes bad or rotten quickly | Costs a lot of money
exercise: «The shop kept its perishables in the cold room.» What are perishables? | Shelves in a shop | Bags for shopping | *Foods that go off quickly | People who work in a shop
exercise: Find and copy one word that is an adjective describing food: «Keep the perishable food in the fridge.» | fridge | the | keep | *perishable
test: In «perishable food», what kind of word is perishable? | Verb | Adverb | *Adjective | Noun
test: Which of these is perishable? | A plastic spoon | A wooden table | *A carton of cream | A tin of beans
exam: Which sentence uses perishables as a noun? | «The perishable milk is in the fridge.» | «Keep the perishable things dry.» | *«The shop kept its perishables in the cold room.» | «The room was very perishable.»
